  "hindi": "कौन सुनेगा — यज्ञ के योग्य जनों में कौन? कौन वन्दनीय देव प्रसन्न होगा? अमरों में किसके हृदय में हम इस देवी को, सबसे प्रिय को, उत्तम स्तुति को, भली-भाँति बुलाई जाने वाली को रखें?",
  "english": "Who will hear, indeed — which one of those worthy of sacrifice? Which worshipful god will take pleasure? In whose heart, among the immortals, may we place this goddess, the dearest, the good praise, well-invoked?",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "kasya taken with hṛdi ('in whose heart'); it could also be construed otherwise (e.g. 'of which one among the immortals'). śreṣāma read as 1 pl. precative/aorist of √śri 'place, lay'. vandāru translated 'worshipful' (adj. from √vand). Notation ṷ in the printed text is edition notation, not a typo. The goddess = the good praise (apposition).",
  "confidence": "medium"
 },
